;; X1 (gym-v2 §3 Group I) — discover-then-aggregate over a SEEDED dataset.
;; A cold agent (never told the :my.subscription/* kind) is asked how much it
;; spends monthly AND which single subscription costs the most. It must
;; DISCOVER the kind (read the store first), SUM the monthly cost (=101), and
;; name the single most expensive (Adobe @45).
;;
;; SINGLE agent over a SEEDED store (deliberately NOT the old A-logs→B-reads
;; shape): pre-seeded fixtures PLUS an agent re-logging the same subscriptions
;; mint DUPLICATE entities, doubling the total (101→202) and silently
;; corrupting the judge. A controlled memory instrument needs ONE unambiguous
;; dataset, so the rows are seeded and a single cold agent analyses them — the
;; same fix x-category-argmax uses. Discovery is preserved: the agent is never
;; told the kind; it must read the store (the inventory block surfaces the
;; attr, a real read still finds the rows). The seeded rows ARE the prior
;; state a previous session left behind.
;;
;; Mechanical legs anchor on op-FAMILIES + attr-name stems (non-fragile §6) +
;; an EXACT row count (a regression that re-introduces a re-log shows as 10,
;; RED, not a silently doubled judge total); the computed total/max lives ONLY
;; on the judge axis with shape-level reference facts.
;;
;; PAID — costs real money. Refused without {:seon.gym/allow-paid? true} +
;; the active provider's API key.
{:seon.gym.scenario/id     :x1-subscriptions-total-and-max
 :seon.gym.scenario/doc    "A cold agent, never told the :my.subscription/* kind, is asked how much it spends on subscriptions monthly AND which single one costs the most. It must discover the kind, SUM the monthly cost (=101), and name the most expensive (Adobe @45) — over a seeded, unambiguous dataset (no re-log double-count)."
 :seon.gym.scenario/tier   :paid
 :seon.gym.scenario/status :active
 :seon.gym.scenario/competency :db-memory
 :seon.gym.scenario/axes   [:consults-findings :replies-honestly :terminates]
 :seon.gym.scenario/schema-registrations
 [[:my.subscription/name [:string {:seon.db/identity true}]]
  [:my.subscription/monthly-usd :int]
  [:my.subscription/category :keyword]]
 ;; Netflix 18 + Spotify 12 + Adobe 45 + iCloud 9 + NYT 17 = 101; max = Adobe @45.
 :seon.gym.scenario/fixtures
 [{:my.subscription/name "Netflix"  :my.subscription/monthly-usd 18 :my.subscription/category :entertainment}
  {:my.subscription/name "Spotify"  :my.subscription/monthly-usd 12 :my.subscription/category :entertainment}
  {:my.subscription/name "Adobe CC" :my.subscription/monthly-usd 45 :my.subscription/category :software}
  {:my.subscription/name "iCloud+"  :my.subscription/monthly-usd 9  :my.subscription/category :storage}
  {:my.subscription/name "NYT"      :my.subscription/monthly-usd 17 :my.subscription/category :news}]
 :seon.gym.scenario/turns
 [{:seon.gym.turn/message "Roughly how much am I spending on subscriptions every month, and which single one costs me the most?"}]
 :seon.gym.scenario/predicates
 [{:seon.gym.predicate/id     :subs-seeded-visible
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :consults-findings
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?e :where [?e :my.subscription/monthly-usd _]]
   ;; EXACTLY 5 — a regression that re-introduces the double-count (an agent
   ;; re-logging the seeded subscriptions) shows up here as 10, RED, not as a
   ;; silently doubled judge total.
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:count 5]}
  ;; DISCOVERY: the agent's first message-driven eval is a seon.db read op —
  ;; the run model scopes "message-driven" on :seon.agent.run/cause (the
  ;; bootstrap run carries no cause), so turn 0 is excluded and this measures
  ;; the agent's first real move.
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id      :discovery-reads-store-first
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind    :first-eval-matches
   :seon.gym.predicate/agent   :a
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis    :consults-findings
   ;; Match the TAUGHT alias form `db/query` (agent home-nses alias
   ;; seon.db :as db — the namespaces manual teaches db/query, db/entity,
   ;; db/transact!) AND the fully-qualified `seon.db/query`. `\bdb/` hits
   ;; both: in `seon.db/query` the `.` is a word boundary before `db`.
   :seon.gym.predicate/pattern "\\bdb/(query|pull|entity|store-inventory)"}
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :replied-to-the-user
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :replies-honestly
   :seon.gym.predicate/args   [:seon.gym.agent/a]
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?m
                               :in $ ?aid
                               :where
                               [?ag :seon.agent/id ?aid]
                               [?m :seon.agent.message/from ?ag]
                               [?m :seon.agent.message/hops ?h]
                               [(pos? ?h)]]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect :non-empty}
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :agent-ends-idle
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :terminates
   ;; idle is DERIVED, never a stored :seon.agent/state datom: an agent is
   ;; idle iff not terminated and owns NO open run (the run's close retracts
   ;; :seon.agent/run → derived :idle). The single agent idle = 1.
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?a
                               :where
                               [?a :seon.agent/id _]
                               (not [?a :seon.agent/terminated-at _])
                               (not-join [?a]
                                 [?r :seon.agent.run/agent ?a]
                                 [?r :seon.agent.run/status :open])]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:count 1]}
  ;; --- judged answer correctness, SEPARATE from the behavior legs ---
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id        :judge-total-and-max
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind      :llm-judge
   :seon.gym.predicate/agent     :a
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis      :replies-honestly
   :seon.gym.predicate/rubric    "PASS only if the reply states a total monthly subscription cost of 101 USD (allow 100-102 for rounding) AND identifies the single most expensive as Adobe (Creative Cloud) at 45. FAIL if there is no total, the total is wrong, or the most-expensive is not Adobe."
   :seon.gym.predicate/reference "The stored rows: Netflix 18, Spotify 12, Adobe CC 45, iCloud+ 9, NYT 17. Sum = 101. Max = Adobe @ 45. These are knowable ONLY by reading the stored subscription rows — a generic guess cannot land the exact total + the exact max."}]}
